1786229750646874	bones-dev	itc:v3:AWKSZJkkk5JkmZMxAAAAQatWqrq1bWwAAAE3Fg		item.create	bn-2y5c	{"description":"Add mouse click-drag text selection to the bones TUI detail pane so users can select and copy bone description text without capturing UI frames, borders, and the list column.\n\nToday the TUI enables mouse capture (crates/bones-cli/src/tui/mod.rs:75), so terminal-native selection is bypassed; shift-drag still works in most terminals but yields a raw screen rectangle including borders.\n\nWork:\n- Pre-wrap detail lines in the app instead of relying on Paragraph::wrap (crates/bones-cli/src/tui/list/render.rs:343) so each cached line maps 1:1 to a screen row. Unicode-aware width.\n- Track Down/Drag/Up in handle_mouse (crates/bones-cli/src/tui/list/input.rs:1294) to maintain an anchor/cursor selection over (line, column).\n- Render the selected range with a reversed/highlight style.\n- Copy the selected text to the clipboard on mouse-up via the existing copy_to_clipboard (crates/bones-cli/src/tui/list/state.rs:9).\n- Fix max_detail_scroll (crates/bones-cli/src/tui/list/data.rs:293) to use the real wrapped line count instead of the naive chars().count().div_ceil(width) estimate.\n- Tests for the wrapper and for coordinate -> text-offset mapping.","kind":"task","title":"TUI: click-drag text selection in the detail pane"}	blake3:UsHtSwuzXC2qq3k7kIx3mIH2fzkTzMxGqXUyh0lcI18
